1
00:00:00,343 --> 00:00:02,418
(Q21（单选）) [课程近况] Hi, Rob. How's the course going?

2
00:00:02,418 --> 00:00:07,958
Oh, hi, Mia. Yeah, great. I can't believe the first term's nearly over.

3
00:00:07,958 --> 00:00:12,193
I saw your group's performance last night at the student theatre.

4
00:00:12,193 --> 00:00:13,618
It was good.

5
00:00:13,618 --> 00:00:14,355
Really?

6
00:00:14,355 --> 00:00:21,398
Yeah ... but now we have to write a report on the whole thing, an in-depth analysis. I don't know where to start.

7
00:00:21,398 --> 00:00:26,287
[角色塑造] Like I have to write about the role I played, the doctor, how I developed the character.

8
00:00:26,287 --> 00:00:28,746
Well, what was your starting point?

9
00:00:28,746 --> 00:00:34,668
Er... my grandfather was a doctor before he retired, and I just based it on him.

10
00:00:34,668 --> 00:00:36,460
OK, but how?

11
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:38,353
Did you talk to him about it?

12
00:00:38,353 --> 00:00:44,043
He must have all sorts of stories, but he never says much about his work, even now.

13
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:47,498
He has a sort of authority though.

14
00:00:47,498 --> 00:00:50,883
So how did you manage to capture that?

15
00:00:50,883 --> 00:00:59,433
I'd ... I'd visualise what he must have been like in the past, when he was sitting in his consulting room listening to his patients.

16
00:00:59,433 --> 00:01:03,149
OK, so that's what you explain in your report.

17
00:01:03,149 --> 00:01:04,531
Right.

18
00:01:04,531 --> 00:01:21,873
[舞台氛围] Then there's the issue of atmosphere - so in the first scene we needed to know how boring life was in the doctor's village in the 1950s, so when the curtain went up on the first scene in the waiting room, there was that long silence before anyone spoke.

19
00:01:21,873 --> 00:01:27,786
And then people kept saving the same thing over and over, like 'Cold, isn't it?'

20
00:01:27,786 --> 00:01:32,369
Yes, and everyone wore grey and brown, and just sat in a row.

21
00:01:32,369 --> 00:01:35,643
Yes, all those details of the production.

22
00:01:35,643 --> 00:01:40,956
[团队协作] And I have to analyse how I functioned in the group - what I found out about myself.

23
00:01:40,956 --> 00:01:44,384
I know I was so frustrated at times, when we couldn't agree.

24
00:01:44,384 --> 00:01:45,629
Yes.

25
00:01:45,629 --> 00:01:48,814
So did one person emerge as the leader?

26
00:01:48,814 --> 00:01:50,031
Sophia did. Sophia

27
00:01:50,031 --> 00:01:54,393
That was OK, she helped us work out exactly what to d， for the production.

28
00:01:54,393 --> 00:01:56,784
And that made me feel better. I suppose.

29
00:01:56,784 --> 00:01:59,185
When you understood what needed doing?

30
00:01:59,185 --> 00:02:02,536
Yes. And Sophia did some research, too.&nbsp;

31
00:02:02,536 --> 00:02:04,906
That was useful in developing our approach.

32
00:02:04,906 --> 00:02:06,284
Like what?

33
00:02:06,284 --> 00:02:16,465
Well, she found these articles from the 1950s about how relationships between children and their parents, or between the public and people like bank managers or the police were shifting.

34
00:02:16,465 --> 00:02:17,970
Interesting.

35
00:02:17,970 --> 00:02:21,791
[技术故障] And did you have any practical problems to overcome?

36
00:02:21,791 --> 00:02:29,964
Well, in the final rehearsal everything was going fine until the last scene - that's where the doctor's first patient appears on stage on his own.

37
00:02:29,964 --> 00:02:31,391
The one in the wheelchair?

38
00:02:31,391 --> 00:02:44,544
Yes, and he had this really long speech, with the stage all dark except for one spotlight - and then that stuck somehow so it was shining on the wrong side of the stage ... but anyway we got that fixed, thank goodness.

39
00:02:44,544 --> 00:02:50,012
Yes, it was fine on the night.

40
00:02:50,012 --> 00:02:55,116
(Q26（配对）) But while you're here, Mia, I wanted to ask you about the year abroad option.

41
00:02:55,116 --> 00:02:57,031
Would you recommend doing that?

42
00:02:57,031 --> 00:02:58,610
Yes, definitely.

43
00:02:58,610 --> 00:03:02,669
It's a fantastic chance to study in another country for a year.

44
00:03:02,669 --> 00:03:08,643
I think I'd like to do it, but it looks very competitive - there's only a limited number of places.

45
00:03:08,643 --> 00:03:17,530
Yes, so next year when you are in the second year of the course, you need to work really hard in all your theatre studies modules.

46
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:24,351
[Q26答案句：E，prove that you know well = show ability] Only students with good marks get places - you have to prove that you know your subject really well.

47
00:03:24,351 --> 00:03:25,342
Right.

48
00:03:25,342 --> 00:03:27,438
(Q27) So how did you choose where to go?

49
00:03:27,438 --> 00:03:40,668
[Q27答案句D，fit in， emphasis on ... rather than ... = relevant] Well.I decided I wanted a programme that would fit in with what I wanted to do after I graduate, so I looked for a university with emphasis on acting rather than directing for example.

50
00:03:40,668 --> 00:03:42,689
It depends on you.

51
00:03:42,689 --> 00:03:50,530
(Q28) Then about six months before you go, you have to email the scheme coordinator with your top three choices.

52
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:57,913
[Q28答案句A， 有朋友miss deadline= be on time] I had a friend who missed the deadline and didn't get her first choice, so you do need to get a move on at that stage.

53
00:03:57,913 --> 00:04:01,459
You'll find that certain places are very popular with everyone.

54
00:04:01,459 --> 00:04:04,675
(Q29) And don't you have to write a personal statement at that stage?

55
00:04:04,675 --> 00:04:05,214
Yes.

56
00:04:05,214 --> 00:04:11,304
[Q29答案句G， get ... to give me tips = ask for help] Right.I'll get some of the final year students to give me some tips, maybe see if I can read what they wrote.

57
00:04:11,304 --> 00:04:13,747
I thinkthat's a very good idea.

58
00:04:13,747 --> 00:04:16,010
I don't mind showing you what I did.

59
00:04:16,010 --> 00:04:19,652
(Q30) And while you're abroad don't make the mistake I made.

60
00:04:19,652 --> 00:04:25,771
[Q30答案句C，arrangement = plan] I got so involved I forgot all about making arrangements for when I came back here for the final year.

61
00:04:25,771 --> 00:04:30,969
Make sure you stay in touch so they know your choices for the optional modules.

62
00:04:30,969 --> 00:04:34,629
You don't want to miss out doing your preferred specialisms.

63
00:04:34,629 --> 00:04:37,129
Right.

